{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/fermata"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV7fermataSayAA10MXLFermataVGvp","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fermata","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFermata","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLFermataV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"fermata","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The fermata signs on either side of the barline, allowing fermatas on both sides (the lower one inverted).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fermata","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFermata","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFermata","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLFermataV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<fermata>"},{"type":"text","text":" elements."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/fermata"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFermata":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfermata","title":"MXLFermata","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFermata","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFermata","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The fermata text content represents the shape of the fermata sign. An empty fermata element represents a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normal fermata. The fermata type is upright if not specified."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFermata"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/fermata":{"title":"fermata","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/fermata","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The fermata signs on either side of the barline, allowing fermatas on both sides (the lower one inverted).","type":